---
import SubLayout from '../layouts/SubLayout.astro';
---

<SubLayout title="FIELD OPERATIONS" section="FIELD OPERATIONS"
  classification="CLASSIFICATION: AUTHORIZED USE ONLY / LAB AND FIELD SCOPE"
  introLines={[
    "These are not hypotheticals.",
    "They are documented patterns.",
    "Scope is the operator's responsibility.",
  ]}
  introAction="[ PROCEED ]">

  <h2>GRID-DOWN COMMUNICATIONS</h2>
  <span class="tag tag--active">AVAILABLE NOW</span>
  <p style="margin-top:0.8rem;">When cell towers are down, WiFi is gone, and internet infrastructure has
  failed, GhostMesh keeps a team coordinated. LoRa mesh radio requires no
  external infrastructure — each node relays traffic for every other node in
  range. Three nodes can cover kilometers of terrain.</p>
  <p>Built-in profiles cover common field status: check-in, moving, hold
  position, medical needed, shelter in place. Custom profiles via SD card
  cover operation-specific callouts.</p>

  <h2>SEARCH AND RESCUE</h2>
  <span class="tag tag--active">AVAILABLE NOW</span>
  <p style="margin-top:0.8rem;">The Hiking/SAR profile provides coordination messages designed for
  search and rescue: trail status, summit reached, camp reached, need water,
  need medical, turning back. Range and battery life make this practical for
  multi-day operations.</p>

  <h2>AUTHORIZED RED TEAM COORDINATION</h2>
  <span class="tag tag--active">AVAILABLE NOW</span>
  <p style="margin-top:0.8rem;">During authorized assessments where cellular and WiFi may be monitored
  or unavailable, GhostMesh provides an out-of-band coordination channel.
  Traffic travels over Meshtastic AES-256 mesh — no cell towers, no WiFi,
  no logs on infrastructure you don't control.</p>
  <p>Private channel required for operational use.</p>

  <h2>DEAD-DROP SURVEILLANCE</h2>
  <span class="tag">PLANNED — PHASE 10–11</span>
  <p style="margin-top:0.8rem;">Deploy the Heltec backpack at a dead-drop location. The node monitors
  the area and broadcasts alerts over LoRa when the zone is disturbed —
  proximity detection, physical disturbance, or case opening. Operates
  fully unattended. Arm/disarm remotely via IR from ~10m. If discovered:
  one action wipes all encryption keys.</p>

  <h2>ENCRYPTION COVERAGE</h2>
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead><tr><th>SEGMENT</th><th>ENCRYPTED</th><th>RISK</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Flipper → Heltec (UART)</td>
        <td style="color:var(--red);">No — Phase 14 planned</td>
        <td>High — physical access</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Heltec → Mesh (default channel)</td>
        <td style="color:var(--terminal);">AES-256 — public key</td>
        <td>Medium — visible to all</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Heltec → Mesh (private channel)</td>
        <td style="color:var(--terminal);">AES-256 — private key</td>
        <td>Low — opaque to outsiders</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>SCOPE</h2>
  <p>All features described here apply only to systems you own or have explicit
  written authorization to test, in controlled lab or field environments, for
  authorized penetration testing or open-source security research. No malware,
  unauthorized access, credential theft, or destructive payloads are implemented,
  planned, or accepted.</p>

  <div class="scene-divider">
    <p>Full use case documentation →
      <a href="https://github.com/ComplacencyKillz/GhostMesh/blob/main/docs/red-team-lab-use-cases.md"
         target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/red-team-lab-use-cases.md</a>
    </p>
  </div>

</SubLayout>
